# Project Instructions for AI Agents

Instructions for AI coding agents working on {{ package_name }}.

This file follows the [AGENTS.md](https://agents.md) convention.
Claude Code reads `CLAUDE.md`, which imports this file through its `@AGENTS.md` line, so
both instruction paths stay aligned.

## Quick Reference

| Task | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Install all deps into `.venv` | `make install` |
| Format and auto-fix (mutates files) | `make fmt` |
| Check everything, like CI (read-only) | `make check` |
| Type check only | `make typecheck` |
| Run tests | `make test` |
| Run one test | `uv run pytest -k "test_name"` |
| Add a dependency | see Dependencies below |
| Build wheel and sdist | `make build` |
| Upgrade deps (respecting the cool-off) | `make upgrade` |

`make` with no target runs install, fmt, check, and test.
What each target does:

```bash
make install     # uv sync --all-extras --all-groups
make fmt         # codespell -w, ruff check --fix, ruff format
make check       # codespell, ruff check, ruff format --check, basedpyright (same as CI)
make test        # uv run pytest
make build       # locked, non-isolated uv build (wheel and sdist)
```

Or call uv directly with the checked-in configuration:
`UV_CONFIG_FILE=uv.toml uv run pytest tests/test_foo.py` or
`UV_CONFIG_FILE=uv.toml uv run python -m {{ package_module }}`.

## Workflow

1. Before starting: `make install` (skip if `.venv` is current).
2. Write or update tests alongside the change; prefer writing the failing test first.
3. After editing: `make fmt` to format and auto-fix.
4. Before committing: `make check` and `make test` must both pass.
   Fix the cause of a type or lint error rather than suppressing it.

## Package Manager

**Strictly use `uv`** for all Python operations: `uv add`, `uv run`, `uv sync`. Never
use `pip`, `pip install`, `python -m pip`, poetry, or `requirements.txt` files.
Run tools through `uv run` (for example `uv run pytest`), not a globally installed copy.

## Conventions

- **Layout**: `src/` layout; code in `src/{{ package_module }}/`, tests in `tests/`.

- **Python**: 3.12+ only; use modern typing: full annotations on every function,
  `list[str]` not `List[str]`, `X | None` not `Optional[X]`, no `from __future__`. Avoid
  `Any` and `# type: ignore` unless truly necessary, and give the rule name when you
  must ignore (`# pyright: ignore[reportFoo]`).

- **Lint/format**: ruff (line length 100) plus codespell; type checking is
  [basedpyright](https://docs.basedpyright.com/). Tool settings live in
  `pyproject.toml`; project-owned uv settings live in `uv.toml`.

- **Tests**: pytest; `test_*` functions in `tests/test_*.py`. Pytest runs in strict
  mode, so register custom markers in `pyproject.toml`.

- **Dependencies**: add with `UV_CONFIG_FILE=uv.toml uv add --exclude-newer "14 days"`
  (runtime) or `UV_CONFIG_FILE=uv.toml uv add --dev --exclude-newer "14 days"` (dev).
  Commit `uv.lock`. Vet new packages first (correct spelling, actually needed); see the
  Supply Chain Hardening section in `docs/development.md`.

- **Versioning**: the version comes from git tags via dynamic versioning; never edit a
  version number in `pyproject.toml`.
  {%- if publish_to_pypi %}

- **Publishing**: releases are published to PyPI by creating a GitHub release tagged
  `vX.Y.Z` (see `docs/publishing.md`).
  {%- endif %}

- **CI**: `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs the `make check` steps and pytest on every
  supported Python version, installing with `uv sync --locked`. If you change
  `pyproject.toml`, re-run `make install` so `uv.lock` stays current.

See [docs/development.md](docs/development.md) for full developer workflows.

